# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating quantum noise in observable expectation value calculations. It works by executing a quantum circuit at increasing noise scales, taking expectation values with respect to those noise scales, and extrapolating to estimate a zero-noise expectation value. Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in different ways. This guide amplifies the noise with \"digital gate folding\", which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^† U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. You can also implement amplification with probabilistic error amplification (PEA), which needs an additional step of learning a noise model and is covered in the [probabilistic error amplification](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning) guide. This guide extrapolates using a couple of built-in fitting strategies (linear and exponential), and it also demonstrates how to implement your own custom fitting function.\n"
msgstr "Ang zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) ay isang teknik para bawasan ang quantum noise sa mga kalkulasyon ng expectation value ng observable. Gumagana ito sa pamamagitan ng pagpapatakbo ng quantum circuit sa tumataas na noise scale, pagkuha ng mga expectation value ayon sa mga noise scale na iyon, at pag-extrapolate para tantiyahin ang zero-noise expectation value. Parehong maipapatupad sa iba't ibang paraan ang mga yugto ng noise amplification at extrapolation. Ina-amplify ng gabay na ito ang noise gamit ang \"digital gate folding\", na nangangahulugang pinapalitan ang mga two-qubit gate ng katumbas na sequence ng gate at ng inverse nito. Halimbawa, ang pagpapalit ng isang unitary $U$ ng $U U^† U$ ay magbibigay ng noise amplification factor na 3. Maaari mo ring ipatupad ang amplification gamit ang probabilistic error amplification (PEA), na nangangailangan ng karagdagang hakbang ng pag-aaral ng noise model at tinatalakay sa gabay na [probabilistic error amplification](/addons/qiskit-mitigation/guides/pea-with-noise-learning). Nag-e-extrapolate ang gabay na ito gamit ang ilang built-in na fitting strategy (linear at exponential), at ipinapakita rin nito kung paano ipatupad ang sarili mong custom na fitting function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind, while ZNE can be effective at mitigating quantum noise for a lower sampling cost than other methods, it comes with no bounds on the bias.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan, bagama't epektibo ang ZNE sa pagbabawas ng quantum noise sa mas mababang sampling cost kaysa sa ibang paraan, wala itong anumang hangganan sa bias.\n"

